WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.460
In 1963, Martin Luther King
gave his I Have a Dream speech.

2
00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:09.380
He hoped his children would be judged
by the content of their character,

3
00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:11.570
not the colour of their skin.

4
00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:16.880
Years before, in 1955, he helped
lead a bus boycott in Montgomery,

5
00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.270
using non-violent protest.

6
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.650
So where did the idea that people
should be judged by character,

7
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.000
not skin colour, come from?

8
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:29.920
In this mission, you'll learn what racism
and racial harmony mean in a multi-ethnic

9
00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.770
society like Britain.

10
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.680
Then you'll see how British law
has tackled racial discrimination,

11
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.520
from 1965 until today.

12
00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:43.470
Your mission: trace where the idea of
judging people by character came from.
